  "rules": [
    "CreateAppContainerProfile must return S_OK before this execution claims profile ownership; ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS fails closed and must never be deleted by this execution.",
    "The PSID returned by CreateAppContainerProfile is released with FreeSid after all uses; do not FreeSid the TokenAppContainer pointer returned inside a GetTokenInformation output buffer.",
    "Token verification requires TokenIsAppContainer == 1 AND a non-null, valid TokenAppContainerSid exactly equal to the newly created profile SID AND TokenIntegrityLevel RID <= SECURITY_MANDATORY_LOW_RID.",
    "SECURITY_CAPABILITIES uses the real profile SID, Capabilities=NULL, CapabilityCount=0, Reserved=0.",
    "InitializeProcThreadAttributeList size probe must fail with ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and a bounded nonzero byte count; allocate, initialize, update, delete, then free in reverse order.",
    "STARTUPINFOEXW.StartupInfo.cb is sizeof(STARTUPINFOEXW), 112 bytes on x64, not sizeof(STARTUPINFOW).",
    "CreateProcessW command-line storage must be writable because Windows may modify it; construct a mutable per-call copy from compiler-owned immutable data.",
    "When PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST is used, CreateProcess bInheritHandles MUST be TRUE and listed handles must be inheritable; without an explicit handle list keep bInheritHandles FALSE.",
    "For every GetTokenInformation call, perform a NULL/zero-length size query, require ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and a nonzero bounded ReturnLength, allocate that size, then verify the returned length is within the allocation before reading fields or SIDs.",
    "Phase 2B.5 is test-fixture-only and must not add production PE imports or call the compiler-emitted broker.",
    "When PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST is supplied, CreateProcessW must use bInheritHandles=TRUE and every listed handle must have HANDLE_FLAG_INHERIT set.",
    "The two parent-side pipe read endpoints must have HANDLE_FLAG_INHERIT cleared; the exact attribute list contains only the stdout and stderr child-side write endpoints.",
    "STARTUPINFOEXW.StartupInfo.dwFlags must include STARTF_USESTDHANDLES and its standard output/error fields must reference the corresponding allowlisted write endpoints.",
    "Drain stdout and stderr concurrently. A blocking read on one pipe while the other pipe is not drained can deadlock when the other pipe buffer fills.",
    "The combined captured byte count, not each stream independently, is bounded to 65536 bytes. Never append beyond the cap.",
    "On cap overflow or any non-EOF pipe-reader failure, terminate the whole Job Object, wait for the root process and job descendants to exit, close all handles, and return bounded partial output with an explicit status.",
    "Only the manifest-hash-pinned child script and fixed absolute System32 PowerShell image may be launched by the test fixture; no model input, arbitrary command, executable, argv, or working directory is accepted.",
    "The Phase 2B.5 fixture inherits the CI environment and runs with the caller token. This does not prove AppContainer integration or clean-environment policy; both remain separate production gates.",
    "The PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST array is sorted in ascending handle-value order before UpdateProcThreadAttribute.",
    "Reader failure test injection must exercise a failed ReadFile call after at least one valid output chunk has already been retained; a failed PeekNamedPipe call alone does not validate the actual stream-read failure path.",
    "SECURITY_ATTRIBUTES.bInheritHandle is a Win32 BOOL and is represented by a signed 32-bit field in the runtime structure manifest.",
    "OutputComplete is true only when both pipe streams reach EOF and the fixed child exits zero; timeout, read failure, and cap overflow return Truncated=true with bounded partial output.",
    "The Phase 2B.5 test invalidates the stdout ReadFile endpoint after at least one valid capture chunk; it must not substitute a PeekNamedPipe-only failure test.",
    "CreatePipe output parameters are indeterminate on FALSE; do not read or close their contents on failure. Only inspect and validate returned handles after TRUE.",
    "The omitted-handle sentinel test compares a 32-byte marker, not a single byte, to avoid treating an unrelated reused handle as proof of inheritance."
  ],
